def second_largest(nums):
    largest = second = None
    for value in nums:
        if largest is None or value > largest:
            if value != largest:
                second = largest
                largest = value
        elif value != largest and (second is None or value > second):
            second = value
    if second is None:
        raise ValueError("No second-largest distinct value")
    return second

The function tracks the largest and second-largest distinct values in one pass, so duplicates of the largest are ignored. It raises ValueError when fewer than two distinct values exist. Time complexity is O(n), with O(1) extra space.
